  "term": "visual pigment",
  "definition": "Visual pigment is a light-sensitive protein complex found in photoreceptor cells. It consists of an opsin linked to a vitamin A–based chromophore, which absorbs light and starts the biochemical process that activates the photoreceptor cell.",
